From 69c3deec2e63810ec61b564f47e3b1a928c0958f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:47:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Rename the distribution to pyqrack-cpu

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/vm6502q/pyqrack/blob/cpu-only/setup.py]

Same rename upstream's own cpu-only branch applies: this is the only
other difference (besides the Makefile's OpenCL flag) between that
branch and main for this release, and matches the real pyqrack-cpu
2.30.6 sdist/wheels already published on PyPI (verified byte-for-byte
identical source tree otherwise).

Building riscv64 wheels under the plain "pyqrack" name would silently
ship something that doesn't match what every other platform gets from
PyPI's pyqrack (which requires a system OpenCL install); using
upstream's own pyqrack-cpu identity instead keeps the package name
truthful about its capability.
---
 setup.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index 9dcbe1d..f692cc9 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ class Build(build_py):
 
 
 setup(
-    name='pyqrack',
+    name='pyqrack-cpu',
     version=VERSION,
     packages=['pyqrack', 'pyqrack.qrack_system', 'pyqrack.stats'],
     cmdclass={"build_py": Build},
-- 
